WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:03.636
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian and actor whose latest

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:06.338
special, "Mohammed in Texas," is
available on Netflix.

00:00:06.338 --> 00:00:09.275
Please welcome to the show
Mo Amer, everybody.

00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:11.644
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:17.617 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:17.617 --> 00:00:23.589 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:23.589 --> 00:00:25.825
Welcome. How are you?
-I'm great.

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:27.360
-This is very exciting.

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.262
Your special takes place --
You shoot it in Texas.

00:00:30.262 --> 00:00:34.367
You grew up in Texas,
but you left Kuwait for Texas.

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:35.634
-Correct.

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:38.137
-That must have been a trip,
as a kid.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:39.572
-We left a big part of it.

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:41.440
We didn't just, like,
voluntarily leave.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:43.443
-Yeah.
-Because of the Gulf War.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.345
-Yes.
-Part one.

00:00:45.345 --> 00:00:46.612
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.612 --> 00:00:48.280
And we ended up
in Houston, Texas.

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.083
-How old were you at the time?
[ Cheers ]

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:52.118
-What's up, H-Town?
People made it.

00:00:52.118 --> 00:00:54.386
Apparently, other people
fleeing Texas as well.

00:00:54.386 --> 00:00:57.389
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:00:57.389 --> 00:00:59.024
-So how old were you
when that happened?

00:00:59.024 --> 00:01:01.995
-I was nine.
-Okay, and so how was Texas?

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:03.195
It must have been
a culture shock.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:04.630
-It was, definitely.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:07.734
My family did no research
when we moved to Houston.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:09.736
-Mm-hmm.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.736 --> 00:01:12.638
-I went to a private British
English school in Kuwait

00:01:12.638 --> 00:01:15.308
and ended up in Houston in
a gang-riddled neighborhood.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:16.476
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.476 --> 00:01:20.179
And I was caught in between
a gang battle.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:21.547
Mexicans were trying to
recruit me

00:01:21.547 --> 00:01:23.249
because they thought
I was Mexican,

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:25.351
and black gangs wanted to
beat me up

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.586
because they thought
I was Mexican.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:28.021
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.021 --> 00:01:30.022
I'd be walking down the street
and I see the Mexican gangs

00:01:30.022 --> 00:01:32.859
hanging out, and they were like,
"Hey, vato.

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:34.761
You walk by here every day.

00:01:34.761 --> 00:01:36.729
You don't say nothing,
don't do nothing.

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:39.332
What? You ashamed of
your own peoples, bro?"

00:01:39.332 --> 00:01:40.967
[ Laughter ]

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:44.103
"You ashamed of your own
la raza, your familia, bro?"

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.271
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:46.939
I'm like, "Nah, man,
my name is Mohammed."

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:51.077
They're like, "What?"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.378
They're like, "For real, bro?

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:54.247
You look exactly like
my cousin Hector!

00:01:54.247 --> 00:01:57.617
No way, bro!"
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.617 --> 00:02:01.487
-And then was it important for
you to shoot this special there?

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.155
-Absolutely, it was
so important.

00:02:03.155 --> 00:02:05.692
I mean, Houston is the city that
raised me and embraced me

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.526
and showed me so much love.

00:02:07.526 --> 00:02:11.464
It was a big, big part of
my life, and I think Houston

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:12.999
doesn't get the flowers
that it deserves.

00:02:12.999 --> 00:02:15.468
So that's why I decided
to shoot it there.

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:17.937
-That's a really nice way
to show some gratitude

00:02:17.937 --> 00:02:19.605
to your hometown,
your adopted hometown.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:21.941
You did a film with The Rock,
and actually,

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:25.277
The Rock, via video, opens this
up for you,

00:02:25.277 --> 00:02:26.946
opens up your special.

00:02:26.946 --> 00:02:29.982
How is it working with The Rock?

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:33.085
-It was good. He was trying to
get bigger for the movie.

00:02:33.085 --> 00:02:37.624
We did the "Black Adam" movie,
and he was just so great, man.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:39.858
He was really gracious.
And like you said,

00:02:39.858 --> 00:02:42.795
he introduced me for my special,
which was so cool.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:45.498
But, you know, he's just
a fun guy, and I didn't know

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:46.966
how much fun he was,
you know what I mean?

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:49.702
Like, you're just on
a superhero set,

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:52.304
and no way you can prepare
for that.

00:02:52.304 --> 00:02:54.207
And he just walks on,

00:02:54.207 --> 00:02:56.242
and he's the only one that
didn't need, like, muscle pants.

00:02:56.242 --> 00:02:59.478
He just walks on
just wearing spandex.

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.915
And everybody is calling him
different names like,

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.450
"What's up, Rock?"
"What's up, D.J.?"

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:06.652
"Hey, Dwayne."
And I walked up to him like,

00:03:06.652 --> 00:03:07.920
"Hey, man, what do I call you?"

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:09.355
He goes, "Daddy."
I was like --

00:03:09.355 --> 00:03:12.759
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.759 --> 00:03:15.061
I just looked at him.
I was like, "Faja?"

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:16.428
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.428 --> 00:03:17.897
"Is that you, faja?"

00:03:17.897 --> 00:03:20.799
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.799 --> 00:03:23.636
I'd get adopted by him,
you know what I mean?

00:03:23.636 --> 00:03:25.304
-I mean, that's the jackpot.

00:03:25.304 --> 00:03:27.306
-Yeah, it would be cheat meals
every day, bro.

00:03:27.306 --> 00:03:29.341
[ Laughter ]

00:03:29.341 --> 00:03:33.112
-I heard a story that you had
a English teacher who was aware

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.281
that you wanted to be up
on stage doing comedy

00:03:35.281 --> 00:03:38.818
and let you use the room
for comedy in return

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.353
for doing some more
scholarly stuff.

00:03:41.353 --> 00:03:43.323
-Yeah, exactly. It was a thing.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:46.358
Like, my dad died when I was 14,
and I was just skipping class.

00:03:46.358 --> 00:03:49.061
I was basically living like
"Ferris Bueller's Day Off."

00:03:49.061 --> 00:03:51.530
I was, like, on third base
watching the Astros.

00:03:51.530 --> 00:03:55.168
I was like 14. I had no business
being there, you know?

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:58.838
And she just was so proactive
and amazing.

00:03:58.838 --> 00:04:00.106
She goes, "Don't you want to be
a comedian?

00:04:00.106 --> 00:04:02.041
Don't you want to graduate
high school?

00:04:02.041 --> 00:04:04.410
How would your father feel
if you don't graduate?"

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:07.880
I'm like, "That's a cold shot,
Mrs. Reed!"

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.515
You know?
[ Laughs ]

00:04:09.515 --> 00:04:12.418
"Yeah, I do."
[ Laughs ]

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:15.187
And she goes, "Well, if you go
up in front of the class

00:04:15.187 --> 00:04:18.891
and recite Shakespeare,
I'll give you extra credit,

00:04:18.891 --> 00:04:21.494
and I'll let you do stand-up
every Friday."

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:24.697
And I was like, "That's a hell
of a bargain."

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.332
I was like, "Do I have to do it?

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:27.967
Like, can I just do it
comically?"

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:29.335
She goes, "You can do it any way
you want."

00:04:29.335 --> 00:04:31.504
So I just went up right in front
of the class.

00:04:31.504 --> 00:04:34.807
I was like -- [Overdramatically]
"To be or not to be.

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:38.611
'Tis is the question."
You know what I mean?

00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:40.412
-I have to ask, did you ever
have a bad set

00:04:40.412 --> 00:04:42.047
with your material
in front of the class?

00:04:42.047 --> 00:04:44.383
-I did. I did. Science class.
It was a rough one.

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:46.619
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.620
-The labs were going,
you know what I mean?

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:50.990
Kids were trying not to burn
themselves.

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.427
I'm trying to do Chris Farley
impressions in front of them.

00:04:54.427 --> 00:04:55.795
[ As Chris Farley ]
"You're going nowhere!"

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.030
You know, like --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:58.030 --> 00:05:01.100
It just didn't work out.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.368
-How does your family --

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:03.836
I mean, they must be so proud of
you now.

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.138
How do they feel when they when

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.372
they get to see you
doing stand-up?

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:07.706
-Oh, they think I'm an engineer.

00:05:07.706 --> 00:05:09.475
-Oh, okay, gotcha.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:12.745
-Will this be the first they --
-This is -- I'm sorry, Mom.

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:17.383
[ Laughter ]
What a failure I am.

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:20.119
No, they're really -- you know,
it's an indigenous art form

00:05:20.119 --> 00:05:21.721
to America, stand-up comedy,
right?

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.889
It's like stand-up,
hip-hop, and jazz.

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.392
And so I never knew it existed.

00:05:26.392 --> 00:05:30.362
So my family, in turn, didn't
really understand

00:05:30.362 --> 00:05:33.933
what was happening, particularly
my mother, and yeah, man.

00:05:33.933 --> 00:05:36.368
She's very proud.
She's very, very proud, yeah.

00:05:36.368 --> 00:05:37.803
I met Steve Harvey,

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:40.072
and that was, like,
the biggest accomplishment.

00:05:40.072 --> 00:05:42.874
Even though I toured with
Chappelle for like 10 years.

00:05:42.874 --> 00:05:44.343
You know, Jon Stewart.

00:05:44.343 --> 00:05:46.112
I've worked with The Rock
and everything else.

00:05:46.112 --> 00:05:48.280
Steve Harvey.
That's it, you know what I mean?

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:52.251
It was like, my mom watches
game shows, that's it.

00:05:52.251 --> 00:05:56.255
"Meeting Steve Harvey, ohh!

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.223
You're really making it now."

00:05:58.223 --> 00:05:59.325
-Well, he's worldwide.

00:05:59.325 --> 00:06:01.927
Steve Harvey is really
a worldwide star.

00:06:01.927 --> 00:06:04.329
Hey, Mo, really great
to meet you.

00:06:04.329 --> 00:06:05.665
Congrats on the special.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:05.665 --> 00:06:07.099
-Thank you for coming out
tonight.

00:06:07.099 --> 00:06:09.135
You guys, that's Mo Amer,
everybody!

00:06:09.135 --> 00:06:12.538
"Mohammed in Texas,"
streaming now on Netflix.

